  (text "J2 (GUITAR_IN): Wire to the input jack: tip -> 1, sleeve -> 2\nR3 (1M): Pull-down: stops a 'pop' when you plug in\nC9 (100nF): Blocks DC from the guitar side\nR4 (1k): With C10: filters radio interference\nC10 (100pF): Ceramic capacitor\nR5 (1M): Biases the op-amp input to VBIAS; 1 MOhm = what a guitar wants to see\nU3 (OPA1678): Dual audio op-amp, rail-to-rail output. NE5532 fits too (same pins, works on 9 V)\nR6 (5.1k): Gain = 1 + R6/R7 = 1.51 (+3.6 dB)\nC11 (100pF): Rolls off gain above 300 kHz (stability)\nR7 (10k): Resistor 0805 1%\nC12 (10uF): Gain only for AC: at DC the stage is a follower and stays at VBIAS\nR8 (1k): Anti-alias filter R (72 kHz with C13)\nC13 (2.2nF): Ceramic capacitor\nC14 (10uF): Blocks VBIAS (4.3 V) from the ADC, which centres itself at 2.5 V\nC15 (1uF): Unused right ADC input: AC-grounded so it stays quiet"
    (at 12 116.02 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.27 1.27))
      (justify left top))
    (uuid "784595b0-d67b-5f6d-b114-1790bb863105"))
  (sheet_instances
    (path "/"
      (page "3"))))
